---
import Eyebrow from "./Eyebrow.astro";
import Screenshot from "./Screenshot.astro";
import untracked from "../assets/untracked.png";
---

<section
  id="how-it-works"
  class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-page flex-col gap-stack px-gutter pt-section"
>
  <Eyebrow>Before the commit</Eyebrow>

  <h2 class="max-w-[880px] font-display text-h2">
    An agent&#39;s output isn&#39;t a commit. It&#39;s a dirty worktree.
  </h2>

  <p class="max-w-[730px] text-body text-muted">
    That is the gap. By the time work has been committed, pushed and opened as a
    pull request, you have already accepted its shape &mdash; and the moment when
    a correction was cheap has passed. GitWarren finds the worktree where the
    branch is checked out, wherever it happens to live on disk, and folds its
    staged, unstaged and untracked files into one diff you can read and comment
    on.
  </p>

  <Screenshot
    src={untracked}
    alt="An untracked file under review, with an agent comment anchored to it"
    caption="A file the agent created and never added to git — reviewed, and commented on, before it was ever a commit."
    class="mt-[28px] max-w-shot max-sm:hidden"
  />
</section>
